---
import PageLayout from '@layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE, LEGAL } from '@config/site';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Editorial Policy"
  description={`${SITE.name}'s standards for sourcing, fact-checking, corrections, AI use and the separation between commercial and editorial decisions.`}
  effectiveDate={LEGAL.effectiveDate}
  lastUpdated={LEGAL.lastUpdated}
>
  <p class="lead">
    This policy describes how {SITE.name} content is produced, reviewed and corrected. It
    exists so readers can audit our process rather than take our word for it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="independence">1. Editorial independence</h2>
  <p>
    Editorial decisions are made independently of commercial relationships. Specifically:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>No vendor receives pre-publication review of any article about their product</li>
    <li>No vendor can pay for inclusion, placement or a higher score</li>
    <li>Advertisers have no input into editorial calendars or conclusions</li>
    <li>
      Writers assign scores before anyone checks whether an affiliate program exists, and are
      not told commission rates
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="sourcing">2. Sourcing standards</h2>
  <p>Every factual claim must be traceable to one of:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Primary testing</strong> — our own hands-on use, with hours logged on the page</li>
    <li><strong>Vendor documentation</strong> — official docs or pricing pages, dated when cited</li>
    <li><strong>Named expert sources</strong> — practitioners identified by name and role</li>
    <li><strong>Published research</strong> — linked directly to the original, never to a summary</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not cite competitor articles as sources of fact, and we do not republish vendor
    marketing claims without independently checking them.
  </p>

  <h2 id="testing">3. Testing requirements</h2>
  <p>
    A product cannot be scored unless a member of our team has used it. For reviews, that
    means a minimum of 20 hours on a paid or full-featured trial plan. Our{' '}
    <a href="/how-we-test/">testing methodology</a> sets out the rubric and weighting.
  </p>
  <p>
    Where we have not tested a product ourselves, we say so explicitly and do not assign a
    score.
  </p>

  <h2 id="fact-checking">4. Fact-checking and review</h2>
  <p>
    All comparison and review content is fact-checked by a second person before publication.
    The fact-checker independently verifies:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Every price against the vendor's live pricing page on the day of review</li>
    <li>Every feature claim against current product documentation</li>
    <li>Every statistic against its cited source</li>
    <li>That pros and cons reflect the testing notes rather than vendor positioning</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The fact-checker is named on the page. Articles display a "Fact-checked by" badge only
    when this review has actually taken place.
  </p>

  <h2 id="review-cycle">5. Update and review cycle</h2>
  <p>
    SaaS pricing changes constantly, so published content is not treated as finished:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Pricing pages and reviews</strong> — re-verified every 90 days</li>
    <li><strong>Integration tutorials</strong> — re-tested every 180 days, or immediately after a vendor UI change</li>
    <li><strong>Comparisons</strong> — re-scored annually, or when a competitor ships a material feature</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The "Last updated" and "Verified" dates on each article reflect real review events, not
    cosmetic edits. We do not bump dates to game freshness signals.
  </p>

  <h2 id="corrections">6. Corrections policy</h2>
  <p>
    When we get something wrong, we fix it and say so. Substantive corrections — anything
    affecting a score, price, recommendation or factual claim — are noted at the foot of the
    article with the date and nature of the change. Typos and formatting fixes are made
    silently.
  </p>
  <p>
    Report an error to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email.editorial}`}>{SITE.email.editorial}</a>.
    We aim to respond within two business days.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai-use">7. Use of AI tools</h2>
  <p>
    We use AI assistance for research triage, outlining and copy editing. We do not publish
    AI-generated articles. Specifically:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Every article is written, edited and signed off by a named human author</li>
    <li>All testing data, scores and screenshots come from actual product use, never generation</li>
    <li>No factual claim enters an article on the authority of a language model</li>
    <li>AI-assisted drafts receive the same fact-checking as any other content</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="authorship">8. Authorship and expertise</h2>
  <p>
    Every article carries a named byline with a linked profile listing the author's relevant
    experience and credentials. We do not use pen names, generic "staff" bylines or fabricated
    author personas. Writers only cover categories where they have direct operating experience.
  </p>

  <h2 id="conflicts">9. Conflicts of interest</h2>
  <p>
    Contributors must disclose any financial interest, employment history or advisory
    relationship with a vendor they cover. Where a conflict exists, either the contributor is
    reassigned or the relationship is disclosed prominently on the article.
  </p>

  <h2 id="sponsored-content">10. Sponsored content</h2>
  <p>
    We do not currently publish sponsored posts, paid guest articles or link insertions. If we
    ever do, such content will be labelled "Sponsored" in the page header, excluded from
    rankings and scored content, and marked with <code>rel="sponsored"</code> on all outbound
    links.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">11. Contact the editorial team</h2>
  <p>
    Editorial Director: Priya Raghunathan —{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email.editorial}`}>{SITE.email.editorial}</a>
  </p>
</PageLayout>
